\subsection{Protocol for reproducibility}
We outline a synthetic study to illustrate BPF estimation and comparisons.
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.4em, itemsep=0.25em]
\item Tasks: synthetic submodular improvement model with diminishing returns; returns sampled from calibrated priors.
\item Methods: Baselines (CoT Greedy; Self-Consistency Majority; a breadth-first Tree-of-Thought baseline), Proposed (IGD), and RS-MCTT (risk-averse variant).
\item Budgets: $B \in \{0,10,20,30,40,50\}$ standardized compute units.
\item Seeds: 50 independent runs per method-budget with a fixed seed schedule.
\item Metrics: estimated $P(B)$, MVC, and reliability (error rate) at fixed $B$.
\item Statistics: report mean $\pm$ 95\% CI (normal approximation or BCa bootstrap); pairwise effect sizes (Hedges' g); Benjamini--Hochberg FDR correction across budgets.
\item Fairness: identical token caps, identical verifier budgets, and identical prompt scaffolds across methods; hyperparameters tuned via nested validation on disjoint synthetic instances.
\end{itemize}

